{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Real.Hyperreal"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.instBlowupFieldHyperreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.instBlowupFieldHyperreal","kind":"instance","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L105-L134","doc":"**De-axiomatisation (bean `zkst`): the hyperreals `ℝ*` are a genuine\n`BlowupField`.** Every field is a Mathlib theorem — `ω = Hyperreal.omega`\nis infinite (`infinitePos_omega`), `st = Hyperreal.st` is additive on the\nfinite (`¬ Infinite`) elements (`Hyperreal.st_add`), fixes real constants\n(`st_id_real`), and kills `ε = ω⁻¹` (`infinitesimal_epsilon`). So the\nblow-up calculus is realisable, not merely axiomatic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.renorm_of_natCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.renorm_of_natCast","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L95-L103","doc":"When the counterterm cancels the divergence exactly down to a\nnatural-number constant `n` — i.e. `X(ω) − C(ω) = n` — the renormalised\nvalue is that constant. The blow-up calculus at work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus.renorm_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus.renorm_def","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Defining identity: `X_ren = st(X(ω) − C(ω))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus.renormalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus.renormalised","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The renormalised real value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus.C","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The counterterm as a function of the cutoff `Λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus.X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus.X","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The divergent expression as a function of the cutoff `Λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus.mk","kind":"ctor","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupCalculus","kind":"structure","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L77-L91","doc":"Data for a blow-up renormalisation over a `BlowupField K`.\n\nA `definition` carrier: the divergent expression `X` and counterterm `C`\nas functions of the cutoff, together with the renormalised real pinned to\nthe standard part of `X(ω) − C(ω)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:surreal-blowup-calculus","label":"def:surreal-blowup-calculus","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-blowup-calculus.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.omega_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.omega_pos","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L70-L73","doc":"`ω` is positive (it exceeds `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.st_epsilon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.st_epsilon","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L67-L68","doc":"The infinitesimal has vanishing standard part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.epsilon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.epsilon","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L64-L65","doc":"The infinitesimal `ε = 1/ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.omega_inv_isFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.omega_inv_isFinite","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The infinitesimal `ε = ω⁻¹` is finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.st_omega_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.st_omega_inv","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The infinitesimal `ε = ω⁻¹` has standard part `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.natCast_isFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.natCast_isFinite","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Natural-number constants are finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.st_natCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.st_natCast","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L52-L52","doc":"`st` fixes the natural-number constants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.st_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.st_add","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L50-L50","doc":"`st` is additive **on finite elements** (it is *not* globally additive;\nno real model of a non-archimedean field is). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.IsFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.IsFinite","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Finiteness predicate (an element with a well-defined standard part). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.st","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.st","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The standard-part retraction onto `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.omega_infinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.omega_infinite","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L43-L43","doc":"`ω` exceeds every natural number — it is infinite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.omega","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The named infinite surreal `ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField.mk","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BlowupField","kind":"class","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BlowupCalculus.lean#L34-L58","doc":"**Blow-up infrastructure.** An ordered field `K` with a named positive\ninfinite element `omega`, a finiteness predicate `IsFinite`, and a\nstandard-part map `st : K → ℝ` that is additive *on finite elements*,\nfixes the natural-number constants, and kills the infinitesimal\n`ε = omega⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}